# Eval fixtures are large and regenerable (eval/make_synthetic_case.py), and
# eval/out/ is scratch: rendered page images and cached raw runs. eval/results/
# is the opposite - small, and the whole point of running the thing - so it is
# committed in full.
eval/cases/fixtures/
# ...except the generated one. It is 273KB, it is ours, and it is what the
# committed accuracy numbers were measured against. It is also not reliably
# regenerable off this machine: make_synthetic_case.py needs a handwriting
# font and only knows Windows paths, so a reviewer on macOS or Linux could
# not rebuild it to check the report.
!eval/cases/fixtures/synthetic.pdf
eval/out/
